From 5945152ffe80ddaf3fcd1da5ce3625c3c202d41c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 18:09:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08123/11362] [outer-loop] Anatomize the ARC induce->plan gate:
 it IS binding, and the rejections are not near-misses

The gate is BINDING, proven at the receiving end rather than by reading the call
site. Injecting the hand-written correct dc22 engine, instrumented plan_in_model
records a call from _induce_and_plan's POST-GATE call site with matching engine
and goal object identity; attempt['planned'] becomes True and policy.plan holds a
step. Nothing downstream drops a gate-passing engine.

But clearing the gate is necessary, not sufficient: the same engine with an
unreachable goal also clears the gate, reaches the same call site, and the planner
returns nothing.

And the rejections are not near-misses. On the 52 of 136 attempts that carry
margins: hidden-state branch median heldout_change_consistency 0.0000, max 0.1781
against a 0.5 threshold, with 16 of 22 at correct_changed_cells == 0 -- failing
the nondegeneracy conjunct at ANY threshold. So a threshold relaxation is not the
lever. Corroborated on the plain branch: a structural nav fit recovering 27-35% of
truly-changed cells scores full-grid exact 0.0000 on tu93 and is rejected
identically to a `return grid` identity engine, while the cell_recall metric that
would separate them already shipped as a flag and already ran as an arm -- still 0
plans installed.

The ~30 unaccounted are 19 generation-side (the LLM never produced a loadable
engine) + 1 goal-side + 10 that CANNOT BE ATTRIBUTED. attempt['skipped'] is written
by the stall refinement loop and only overwritten when the plain gate REJECTS, so
an attempt that CLEARS the gate and whose planner finds nothing keeps the stale
refinement label. Demonstrated live, and witnessed in the corpus itself: two
records labelled no_reachable_plan_after_refinement carry verify_accuracy 0.96/0.92
-- they passed. ft09's surviving on-disk engine is `return grid` on every branch
with is_level_complete -> False, which is exactly that shape.

Also: the 63/43 split is not two kinds of engine failure, it is the
HIDDEN_STATE_GAME_IDS partition; and the 136 pools two arms whose generator was
broken (0 planned survives restriction to the 88 valid-row attempts).

No GPU, no GGUF, no generator. Nothing tracked was written -- load_engine is
monkeypatched, so results/arc_e3 is untouched. Re-run from the formatted script
reproduces every substantive value (17 differing leaves, all timing/checksum).

